{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"wc -l docs/design/yang.preludes.md && rg -n '\"'^#|r8|H[1-8]|M9|Track B|P[0-4]′'\"' docs/design/yang.preludes.md\"","aggregated_output":"679 docs/design/yang.preludes.md\n5:# yang.preludes: configurable and composable preludes for Yang frontends\n7:**Status:** Proposed design, 2026-11-21 (r8 — r7 reconciliation: selector, entry ABI, effect unwind, role evidence, slice repair). No implementation or completed acceptance gate is claimed.\n15:- **2026-11-21 (r7 → r8 reconciliation):** Addressed all findings from the r7 architect review (thread `01a1faa3-bb7e-7c30-b3bf-cedbad008bfc`; 8 HIGH, 1 MEDIUM, plus default-profile regressions): (H1) explicit default-selector mechanism — the composition's immutable configuration carries the preferred `[id revision]`, applied at the normal request entry, with two-revision / legacy-pin / in-flight-snapshot gates; (H2) per-frontend **entry-lowering contracts** emitting the landed native entry shapes (`py` 1-arg `run-main`, `js` 1-operand, `php` 2-or-4 with request stream) alongside the Clojure resolver-bearing 2-arg shape; (H3) ONE derivation record (frontend/lowerer revision, descriptor, resolved runtime closure, input, output), pins reconciled by module symbol before lowering, dependency-first installation in linked composition, resolver derivation in provenance / live cell in the task; (H4) complete effect-unwind traversal per frame kind with exactly-once cleanup, a P2′ cold-error policy for plain `yang.clojure`, `clojure.core.impl` owning zero cells while declaring its runtime effects; (H5) address-bound export-**role** evidence (same-arity wrong-role fails closed); (H6) the §5.1 example labeled a Track B recipe recording bundled shape, linked trailing forms, pins, and C1 behavior independently; (H7) slice repair — P1′ clj-only synthetic fixtures, P2′ native collection invocation + bundled shadowing, P3′ the real cross-syntax unwind; (H8) boxed conversion/true-division at the host boundary, zero-raw-double scoped to boxed-path profiles; (M9) `yang.core.defquoted` naming consistency, r6 gates attached verbatim to Track B, oracle assignment (legacy pins ← native oracles, default ← capability refusals); (R) default-profile regressions — unqualified `:k` admission, cross-carrier integer identity, `:clj/unbound` distinguishability, canonical order settled to Jing encoded-byte order.\n24:## 1. Problem statement and repository baseline\n26:### 1.1 Current repository baseline\n48:### 1.2 Three problems to solve together\n56:## 2. Derivation from foundations and non-negotiable invariants\n60:### 2.1 Foundational axioms & three-tier hybrid rationale\n74:### 2.1a Alignment with the tao architecture's second axiom (`yang.tao.md` §2.2)\n84:### 2.2 Non-negotiable invariants\n103:## 3. Three-tier hybrid architecture & prelude layering\n134:### 3.1 Litmus test: Native Host `:pure` vs. Guest `%capture` Effects vs. VM Effects\n142:### 3.2 Explicit exclusions from Layer 2a (`yrt.*`)\n156:## 4. Host `:pure` core extensions & Layer 2a (`yrt.*`) specifications\n158:### 4.1 Native host `:pure` core extensions (`data`, `float`, `kind`)\n172:   - **`data/canonical-compare [a b]`:** Total, deterministic comparator over admitted keys/elements. **Normative order (r8):** delegates to the host canonical ordering kernel matching `dao.jing.cbor.md:173`'s unsigned encoded-byte order (which places `0` before `nil` — the r7 type-rank list was wrong and is withdrawn), with recursive lexicographic comparison for compound values; identical results on all 4 hosts.\n174:2. **Boxed IEEE-754 host module `yin.vm.float` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/float.cljc`, module name `'float`):** **Host-boundary conversion rule (r8):** boxed conversion and true-division results are exposed AT the host boundary (`integer/to-float` results and `true-div` quotients enter guest frames only as boxed `data/float64`); the zero-raw-double guarantee is scoped to profiles on the boxed path (the Clojure-family profiles). The frozen native ABI of the legacy preludes is unchanged.\n185:### 4.2 `yang.call` *(existing Layer-2a leaf)*\n189:### 4.3 `yrt.effect` — Unified guest algebraic effects over `%capture`\n205:- **Unwind traversal semantics (r8):** `raise` delivers to the first non-`:finally` boundary; on the way down every `:finally` frame runs its cleanup closure **exactly once**, and every `:effect` frame is popped with its context restored (an `:effect` frame carries no cleanup closure — a guest throw crossing an unrelated effect handler is a plain unwind past it, never an error). `perform` walks `ctx-cell` to the nearest matching `:effect` frame **without** running `:finally` frames; only when the handler aborts without resuming does the abort path run the traversed `:finally` cleanups during that unwind. In all cases the context is restored to the surviving frame's state and each cleanup runs at most once per activation.\n224:  3. **Generators / coroutines (Track B — deferred):** `yield` is simply `(yrt.effect/perform ctx :gen/yield value)` handled by a coroutine driver that stores the captured continuation `k` and resumes `(k sent-val)` on `.next()`/`.send()`, with explicit `on-start-ctx` / `on-resume-ctx` hooks preserving Python `:base` rebasing vs. PHP direct context restoration and refcount cleanup.\n225:  4. **Safepoint interrupts (Track B — deferred):** `yrt.safepoint` polls `stream/poll!` (VM effect) and performs `:runtime/interrupt` via `yrt.effect` when a signal arrives (Python maps to `KeyboardInterrupt` / registered signal handler; JS maps to uncatchable root unwind).\n230:### 4.4 `yrt.int` — Exact-integer adapters and radix scanners\n241:### 4.5 `yrt.safepoint` *(Track B — deferred)*\n247:## 5. Declarative prelude composition, recipes, and admission\n251:### 5.1 Emission recipe vs. resolved runtime profile\n300:### 5.2 Composition rules and verified-closure admission\n313:## 6. Preludes as swappable libraries: the semantics descriptor contract\n315:### 6.1 Focused profile scope: Yin/Clojure DEFAULT + Native legacy track\n324:### 6.2 Core vs. Frontend ownership boundary\n335:### 6.3 Portable `:yang.semantics/descriptor` schema\n467:### 6.4 Validation, lexical hygiene, authority checks, and parameterization\n478:4. **Address-bound export-role evidence (r8):** qualification, closure membership, and arity alone do not establish a hook's *role* — a binary `clj/prim-get` satisfies an arity check for `:op/add`. The frontend contract or the admitted profile therefore supplies per-hook **role records** (arity + role: `:cell-accessor`, `:value`, operator, projection) resolved by recorded address, and host primitive profiles are resolved by their recorded profile addresses. A same-arity wrong-role target fails closed.\n480:6. **Frontend parameterization:** `yang.python.antlr.lower`, `yang.typescript.antlr.lower`, and `yang.php.antlr.lower` read literals, hooks (including 2-arg `:unit/run-main [body-fn ambient-resolver]` and optional `:comp/finish`), capabilities, and projections from `:yang.semantics/descriptor`, preserving full CPython/Node/PHP oracle and 4-host parity under the legacy pins. **Entry-lowering contracts (r8):** each frontend's contract specifies BOTH entry shapes — the landed native entry shape (`py/run-main` 1-arg, `js` single-operand, `php` 2-or-4 with the request stream in slot two) for the legacy track, and the Clojure profile's resolver-bearing 2-arg `[body-fn ambient-resolver]` shape — so the native mapping is 1:1 against the FROZEN exports and never re-arches them to satisfy the Clojure profile. **Oracle assignment (r8):** native-oracle parity suites gate the LEGACY pins; capability-refusal suites gate the default profile.\n482:### 6.5 Frontend SPI and provenance integration (`yang.frontend`)\n486:- `:yang.frontend/lowering-profile` pins the content address of the `:yang.semantics/descriptor` EDN artifact; `:yang.frontend/runtime-profile` pins the resolved `:yang.prelude/profile` manifest. **Descriptor/runtime reconciliation (r8):** where two lowerer revisions consume one descriptor, the pins are reconciled **by module symbol before lowering** — a conflicting pin fails closed. Dependency-first module installation belongs to linked composition (a verified dependency pin does not install its module in a cold task; first execution on a cold task is gated). The resolver's derivation is recorded in provenance; its live cell is task-owned.\n487:- Compilation provenance retains the exact derivation record (r8: frontend/lowerer revision, descriptor, resolved runtime closure, input, output).\n488:- **Default selector (r8):** the composition's immutable configuration carries the preferred `[frontend-id revision]` pair, applied at the normal request entry; `yang.frontend/select`'s ID-only ambiguity resolves through that configuration. Gates: both revisions installed → ordinary request selects Clojure semantics; explicit legacy pin → native behavior preserved; in-flight request → original snapshot retained.\n492:## 7. Case study: `yang.python` with a `clojure.core` prelude (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`)\n494:### 7.1 Value representation & semantic mapping\n513:### 7.2 Portable numeric & collection contract (`clj.py` over `:pure` host core + `yrt.effect`)\n526:   - Exact ints promote via `(data/float64 (yrt.int/check-limit (clj/rt-ctx) (integer/to-float-boxed i)))` — `integer/to-float-boxed` (r8) returns the boxed carrier at the host boundary so no raw host double crosses a guest frame.\n534:### 7.3 Python lowering Hook ABI & `clj.py` adapters\n553:### 7.4 Unified trusted `clj` callable bridge, cross-unit admission, and §8.10.7 validation\n568:### 7.5 Two-module portable `clojure.core` contract (`clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core`)\n573:   - Requires `yang.call`, `clj`, `yrt.int` (zero direct provenance doors; **zero state cells — but it DECLARES its runtime effects**: the `:coll/unsupported-key` and `:int/*` effects its definitions perform are part of its declared footprint, installed by the owning entry's policy handlers — `clj.py/run-main` at P3′, plain `yang.clojure`'s own cold-error policy at P2′). Host dependencies: `kind` (with `kind/namespace`), `data` (with `float64?`, `equiv`, `admit-key?`, `canonical-compare`, `canonical-entries`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), `float`, and `cell` (for cell checks/updates only).\n588:### 7.6 Concrete lowering example\n606:## 8. Portability, content addressing, and malleability\n608:### 8.1 Multi-host portability (JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, Jolt/Scheme)\n610:- **ClojureDart AOT literal limits:** Consolidate `defquoted` into **`yang.core.defquoted`** (r8 M9 — the dedicated host macro namespace; NOT `yang.core.prelude`, keeping the emission namespace free of macro definitions).\n615:### 8.2 Dependency graph and malleability (`docs/agents/malleability.md`)\n633:### 8.3 Content-addressing and golden discipline (Clean-Slate)\n639:## 9. Phased implementation roadmap and acceptance gates\n641:**r7 reordering (owner directive D10 — Clojure-first):** the Clojure prelude family is built FIRST; the native py/js/php preludes are untouched by these slices (frozen as landed, zero golden churn), with their `yrt.*`/boxed-float re-architecture deferred to the legacy track (Track B). The original r6 P1–P4 order is superseded; its non-Clojure legs reappear in Track B.\n645:| **P0′ — Composition plumbing & `:pure` host core extensions** | Implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` / `:yang.prelude/profile`, `validate-profile` + `admit-profile` **in `yang.core.prelude-admission`** (3→5 publics, per the §5.2 home rule); add `:pure` host exports (`data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `kind/namespace`, and boxed `yin.vm.float` across all 4 hosts); consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.defquoted` (dedicated host macro namespace, keeping `yang.core.prelude` at 11 publics — naming per r8 M9, consistent across §8.1/§8.2); base-prelude emitter recipes record the *current* per-prelude modes as migration truth (`:linear` for `py`, `:balanced` for `php`/`js`/`clj`-family) without changing shapes. | No golden churn for py/js/php (no shape change); new modules get fresh addresses | Closure, missing-manifest, `host-limits`, direct-provenance vs. transitive-footprint tests; 4-host test suite for `data/equiv` (`[0.0] == [-0.0]`, `[NaN] != [NaN]`, `(keyword nil \"a/b\") != (keyword \"a\" \"b\")`), `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`/`canonical-entries`, and `yin.vm.float` (`2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0`, `-0.0 // 2.0 == -0.0`, `0.5 ** -2000 -> :underflow`, `format` `1.0 -> \"1.0\"`); existing py/php oracle suites unchanged-green. |\n646:| **P1′ — `yrt.effect` + `yrt.int` with Clojure-only consumers; unified trusted `clj`** | Implement stateless `yrt.effect` (5-slot `data/nth` frames, abortive `raise`/`try-value`/`try-orelse`/`try-finally`/`call-ec`, plus resumable `handle`/`perform` — the frame design anticipates py/php `:depth` accounting but only clj/clj.py exercise it) and `yrt.int`; upgrade `clj` to the unified trusted form (two-step `make-callable`, evaluated `assoc` conditions, `invoke-callable`, `prim-get`/`prim-assoc`, retiring `yang.clojure`'s `dsg__call_token` / inline provenance ops); add `dsg__add`/`dsg__lte` for bundled `clj`. **py/js/php preludes untouched** — they keep their own mechanisms. | Refresh `clj`/`yang.clojure` goldens cleanly; py/js/php goldens untouched | `yrt.effect` unit tests (abortive, `finally`, resumable one-shot `handle`/`perform`, cold policy traps) across semantic/stack/register VMs; bundled/linked `yang.clojure` parity under shadowed `(defn get ...)`; clj-only synthetic nonzero depth/base fixture fixtures exercising the `:depth` slot (H7 slice repair); independent concurrent `clj` tasks sharing `yrt.*`; bundled == linked + 4-host; `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` clean. Native collection invocation and bundled primitive shadowing through the new standard library gate at P2′; the REAL cross-syntax `clj → clj.py → clj` unwind with cleanup and context restoration gates at P3′. |\n647:| **P2′ — Unified `clojure.core` + `yang.clojure` migration** | Publish collision-free `clojure.core.impl` (pure, `impl-*` prefix, `admit-key?`-guarded) + cell-free `clojure.core` facade; migrate `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core`. | Refresh `yang.clojure` goldens cleanly | Authenticated callable cells returning `false` for all collection predicates; two-step `make-callable` + §8.10.7 condition fidelity; bundled == linked parity for nested `clj → clj.py → clj` unwinds; unified `yang.clojure` suite green. |\n648:| **P3′ — Descriptor parameterization + `clj.py` + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (the DEFAULT flip)** | Implement generic `yang.core.semantics` with UAST-derived arity & role validation; define the python frontend contract; refactor `yang.python.antlr.lower` to read literals/hooks/capabilities from `:yang.semantics/descriptor` (the legacy `py-v1` descriptor pins today's `'py/*` hooks 1:1 — behavior-preserving, gated by the existing CPython oracle suites); publish `clj.py`; flip `yang.python`'s default `runtime-profile` to `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (a revision re-pin in `yang.frontend`). | py goldens regenerate under the descriptor-driven path (legacy descriptor byte-identical outcomes); clojure-core-v1 gets fresh goldens | Legacy-descriptor behavior preservation: full CPython corpus + 4-host parity under `py-v1` pin; end-to-end 4-host `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` suite (numeric/float ops, `:max-bits 53` limit traps, `data/admit-key?` refusals, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-entries` ordering, deterministic `str`/`gensym`); capability refusal tests (typed `except E:`, `genexpr` under `:control/generators :refused`); default-profile regressions (r8): an unqualified `:k` key admits successfully (the namespace-non-empty rule applies to two-part keywords only); equal exact integers in different host carriers hit the same map entry on insert AND lookup; a local/projected value equal to `:clj/unbound` remains distinguishable from an absent binding; canonical traversal order matches Jing encoded-byte order (`0` before `nil`); UAST-derived validation rejecting wrong arity, non-lambda hooks, unqualified hooks, reserved doors, out-of-closure exports. |\n649:| **P4′ — Additional N → 1 profiles** | `:yang.typescript/clojure-core-v1` next (descriptor + ts frontend contract); `:yang.php/clojure-core-v1` after. | Fresh goldens per profile | End-to-end parity suites per profile. |\n650:| **Track B — Legacy prelude re-architecture (deferred, on demand)** | Migrate the native `py`/`js`/`php` preludes onto `yrt.effect`/`yrt.int`/boxed float (the r6 P1/P4 legs: 4→5-slot contexts, generators via `:gen/yield`, `yrt.safepoint`, `php.sp` integration per its own hooks); undertaken only when legacy demand justifies it. | Refresh py/js/php goldens per migration slice | The r6 P1/P4 gates apply verbatim at that time, attached here by value: generator + safepoint parity suites across VMs/hosts preserving PHP lifecycle/cleanup and Python `:base` rebasing; migration of `py`/`js`/`php` onto `yrt.effect`, `yrt.int`, and boxed `yin.vm.float` (4→5-slot contexts; `dsg__add`/`dsg__lte` for bundled `clj`); existing Python & PHP generator tests green; independent concurrent `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj` tasks sharing `yrt.*`; bundled == linked + 4-host + CPython/Node/PHP oracle parity; `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` clean. |\n654:## 10. Owner decisions and disposition ledger\n656:1. **D10 — Default-profile policy & legacy-track deferral (`Settled — r7 Owner Directive`):** For the parameterized frontends, the **Yin/Clojure profile is the DEFAULT** (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` first; ts/php to follow); the native preludes (`py`/`js`/`php` semantics) become the **Legacy compatibility track** — kept frozen as landed (they already exist at their current content addresses with passing oracle suites), with their `yrt.*`/boxed-float re-architecture deferred to Track B until legacy demand justifies it. The clojure prelude family is built first. Consequence named in §6.1: capability refusals (classes, generators, typed `except`, `with`, kwargs) are the default experience for source written against native semantics; pinning the legacy revision is the escape hatch.\n663:3. **D3 — Python float tagging (r7: moot until Track B — py keeps its tagged `{:py/float}` representation as-frozen; boxed `yin.vm.float` ships for the Clojure path in P0′):**\n673:7. **D7 — Float exponentiation rounding (r7: `fpow-half` ships in P0′ for the Clojure path; `fpow-base` defers to Track B with the php re-architecture):**\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
