{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '60,99p;160,181p;192,220p;249,311p'\"","aggregated_output":"    60\t### 2.1 Foundational axioms & three-tier hybrid rationale\n    61\t\n    62\t1. **Everything is a Stream:** Prelude selection, composition, and lowering are pure functions of explicit data configurations and CST streams. External I/O and host capabilities remain declared VM/stream effects (`stream/*`, `cell/*`, `:module/require`) per ADR 0004; prelude composition adds no ambient I/O.\n    63\t2. **Interpretation Creates Semantics:** A CST packet carries syntax only; its runtime meaning emerges from `(cst-packet, lowering-profile, semantics-descriptor, runtime-profile)`. Interpreting one Python CST under `:yang.python/py-v1` (CPython semantics) versus `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (Clojure persistent-data semantics) is a direct realization of \"one truth, many perspectives.\"\n    64\t3. **Code and State are Datoms (and Unitarity / Derive-Don't-Persist):**\n    65\t   - Lowering preserves source CST identity; compiled UAST roots under different preludes have distinct content addresses (or identical addresses when two descriptors emit identical UAST) linked by explicit provenance datoms pinning `(cst-address, lowering-profile, semantics-descriptor, runtime-profile, unit-address)`.\n    66\t   - Zero new AST tags, zero VM opcodes, and zero manifest schema changes are introduced. Linker manifests retain schema 1, and C1 `:yang/call-site` tables continue to publish beside manifests rather than inside them.\n    67\t   - Composition facts (which `yrt.*` modules a prelude requires) live in the explicit module `:requires` DAG, never as a redundant tag in UAST rows.\n    68\t4. **Everything is a Continuation (Hybrid Effect Boundary):**\n    69\t   Real-world algebraic-effect systems converge on one clean boundary: **Unison** keeps pure built-in value types (`Nat`/`Int`/`Float`/`Text`/`Bytes`) in the runtime, models control/errors/streams as pure user-handled abilities, and reserves only `IO` for the runtime; **Koka** keeps total math/data primitives effect-free (`total`) and draws the effect line at partiality (`exn`), divergence (`div`), state (`st`), and I/O; **OCaml 5** keeps hot synchronous ops native, reserves effect handlers for resumable control flow, and forbids effects from crossing raw native/C frames. Yin/Yang adopts the exact same three-tier split:\n    70\t   - **Pure host value core (`:pure` primitives):** Total, representation-sensitive math, equality, canonical ordering, key admission, and text ops stay native and fast across all 4 hosts.\n    71\t   - **Guest algebraic effects (`yrt.effect` over `%capture`):** Control flow (exceptions, `finally`, PHP `abandon-to`, resumable `yield`) and cold policy traps (`:math/div-zero`, `:math/overflow`, `:int/bit-limit`, `:int/digit-limit`, `:coll/unsupported-key`, `:runtime/interrupt`) live in pure guest UAST — zero Jolt kernel expansion.\n    72\t   - **VM / stream effects (`make-effect` → `:effect-handlers`):** Strictly `cell/*`, `stream/*`, `:module/require`, and bound external surfaces per ADR 0004.\n    73\t\n    74\t### 2.1a Alignment with the tao architecture's second axiom (`yang.tao.md` §2.2)\n    75\t\n    76\tThe semantics descriptor and profile pinning are a direct application of the governing axiom **Everything is a Stream** and its invariant *Do not introduce callbacks; every callback is an event on a stream*:\n    77\t\n    78\t- **Interpreter configuration is stream-resident data.** `yang.tao.md` §2.2 requires that \"the grammar, name environment, and elaborator configuration participate in interpretation\" and that \"an interpretation result must name both its input and the interpreter that produced it.\" The hardcoded `py/*`-style coupling in the current lowerers buried that configuration in host code; the `:yang.semantics/descriptor` and `:yang.prelude/profile` lift it into portable, content-addressed artifacts, and the compilation **derivation record** names the interpreter exactly: `(frontend/lowerer revision, descriptor address, resolved runtime closure, input address, output address)` — one record, consistent with `yang.antlr.md`'s compilation derivation contract; the resolver's *derivation* belongs in provenance while its *live cell* belongs to the task.\n    79\t- **\"One truth, many perspectives\" is a stream operation.** The same Python CST packet is one truth; `py-v1` and `clojure-core-v1` are two perspectives. Selecting between them — the wolf-in-sheep's-clothing inversion — is a *re-pin of stream-resident artifacts* (the descriptor and profile addresses), never a callback into the lowerer and never ambient prelude state.\n    80\t- **The \"explicit local functions\" clause is where the ambient resolver lives:** the `:kind :cell-accessor` projections resolve through the unit-bound `ambient-resolver` passed as data (`[body-fn ambient-resolver]`) — a task-local cell of cells, explicit, named in the provenance, and validated against verified UAST before use.\n    81\t\n    82\tConsequence: switching a frontend's default semantics is a *data re-pin* (revision selection in `yang.frontend`), carrying zero code change and zero content-address churn for unselected profiles.\n    83\t\n    84\t### 2.2 Non-negotiable invariants\n    85\t\n    86\t1. **No hidden global state — stateless `yrt.*` modules:**\n    87\t   - `yang.core.*` holds no mutable global registry of preludes or languages (`yang.frontend` immutable catalog rule).\n    88\t   - **Shared `yrt.*` modules own zero `*.rt/*` state cells.** Every stateful `yrt.*` function takes the caller's task-local state cell (e.g., `ctx-cell`) as an explicit parameter. When a single Yin task links independent foreign language runtimes (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj`) together via `yang.call`, each foreign runtime maintains its own isolated handler stack and depth/base accounting inside its own `*.rt/ctx` cell rather than aliasing or corrupting another language's stack.\n    89\t   - **Intentional intra-Clojure domain sharing:** By explicit architectural design, `clj`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core.impl`, and `clojure.core` execute *inside* the Clojure semantics and exception domain and therefore share `(clj/rt-ctx)` intentionally so Clojure `(throw ...)` / `(try ... (finally ...))` and Python-syntax `try` / `except` / `finally` unwind across `clj → clj.py → clj` nesting on one coherent handler stack while saving and restoring `(clj/rt-ctx)` at every `yrt.effect/try-value` and `finally` boundary.\n    90\t2. **No implicit control flow:** All escapes and resumptions remain explicit continuation invocations over an explicit handler chain.\n    91\t3. **No raw callbacks & no raw host doubles in guest frames:** Policy handlers and closures passed into `yrt.*` are ordinary guest Yin closures, never host-boundary callbacks. By boxing IEEE-754 float operations at the `yin.vm.float` host boundary, unwrapped host doubles never appear on guest stacks, making `%capture` and safepoints safe everywhere.\n    92\t4. **No shared mutable state:** Each stateful profile allocates its own task-local cells once per task in its own idempotent `init!` under its own private namespace (`py.rt/*`, `js.rt/*`, `php.rt/*`, `clj.rt/*`, `clj.py.rt/*`, `clojure.core.rt/*`); `clojure.core.impl` is pure and stateless.\n    93\t5. **No layer collapsing:** Parsing (host ANTLR boundary) → lowering (syntax + frontend lowering contract + semantics descriptor → UAST) → prelude composition & admission (pure spec/artifact verification; never publishes or executes) → publication/linking → VM execution stay separated across explicit stream/module boundaries.\n    94\t6. **No assumed graphs:** Every composed prelude declares an explicit, acyclic `:requires` DAG over an **immutable, verified artifact closure**. Missing exports, missing transitive artifacts, or cycles fail closed at validation/admission time before publication or execution.\n    95\t7. **No closed language registry (`yang.antlr.md` owner directive):** Neither `yrt.*` nor `yang.core.*` contains a `case`/dispatch over `:python`, `:typescript`, `:php`, or `:clojure`, inspects `:py/type`/`:js/type`/`:php/type`/`:clj/type` tags, or encodes language-specific lowering ABI tables.\n    96\t8. **Security boundary — VM provenance doors stay private:** Under `src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md` and `src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc`, `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and `cell/dsg__provenance` are reserved compiler/runtime-module doors whose names guest code must not forge or re-export.\n    97\t   - **`yrt.*` modules, `clj.py`, and Layer-2c standard libraries (`clojure.core.impl`, `clojure.core`) MUST NEVER declare (`:yin.module/primitives`) or export (`:yin.module/exports`) provenance-door primitives directly.** (Transitive `:yin.module/footprint` unions are governed by `:yang.prelude/max-effects`.)\n    98\t   - **No descriptor hook or source-facing ambient projection** may expose `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, `yang.safepoint/*`, or non-projectable internal implementation modules such as `*.impl/*` (`clojure.core.impl/*`) (`§6.3`).\n    99\t   - Retained protocol-condition provenance (`yang.antlr.md` §8.10.7) resides strictly inside trusted Layer-2b runtime modules (`py`, `js`, `php`, **`clj`**) in **both** bundled (`uast`) and linked (`module-uast`) emission, never exported and never exposed across `yrt.*`, Layer-2c libraries, or source scope.\n   160\tExisting `yin.vm.integer` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc`, v4) and `yin.vm.data` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc`) already establish the `:pure` host-module pattern: total or keyword-status-returning kernels over `dao.host.*` and `dao.jing.cbor` with zero guest callbacks and identical semantics across JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, and Jolt/Scheme.\n   161\t\n   162\tTo eliminate host representation leaks and raw-double stack-frame hazards across all frontends, we add a small, cohesive set of `:pure` exports (zero changes to VM opcodes or `yin.vm/primitives`):\n   163\t\n   164\t1. **Additions to `yin.vm.data` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc`):**\n   165\t   - **`data/float64? [x]`:** Backed directly by existing `dao.jing.cbor/float64?` (`src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:212`). Distinguishes float64 carriers from exact integers, booleans, and maps on all 4 hosts.\n   166\t   - **`data/equiv [a b]`:** Portable IEEE-aware, kind-strict value equality (distinct from content-addressing `data/content=`):\n   167\t     - Exact int × exact int: `integer/compare == 0`; float64 × float64: `false` if either is `NaN`, else IEEE numeric equality (`+0.0 == -0.0` is `true`, `NaN == NaN` is `false`); exact int × float64: **`false`** (`1 != 1.0`).\n   168\t     - Keywords/symbols: strict kind + nullable namespace + name equality, so `(keyword nil \"a/b\") == (keyword \"a\" \"b\")` is **`false`** on CLJS/Node as well as JVM/Dart/Jolt.\n   169\t     - Persistent vectors/lists, maps (excluding `:cell-ref` handles), and sets: recursive pairwise/entry equality using `data/equiv`.\n   170\t     - Other scalars (`nil`, booleans, strings, authenticated `:cell-ref` handles): host `=`.\n   171\t   - **`data/admit-key? [k]`:** Recursive portable key/element predicate preventing host map/set collapse (`yin/vm/data.cljc:34–36`, `dao.jing.cbor.md:173, 266`). Returns `true` iff `k` (recursively across vectors, maps, and sets) contains only `nil`, booleans, exact integers, strings, and unambiguous keywords/symbols (`ns` non-empty and free of `\"/\"`, `name` free of `\"/\"` and not starting with `\":\"`); returns `false` for any `float64?` (at any nesting depth), ambiguous identifiers, seqs/lists, closures/continuations, or `:cell-ref` handles.\n   172\t   - **`data/canonical-compare [a b]`:** Total, deterministic comparator over admitted keys/elements. **Normative order (r8):** delegates to the host canonical ordering kernel matching `dao.jing.cbor.md:173`'s unsigned encoded-byte order (which places `0` before `nil` — the r7 type-rank list was wrong and is withdrawn), with recursive lexicographic comparison for compound values; identical results on all 4 hosts.\n   173\t   - **`data/canonical-entries [coll]`:** For a map, returns a vector of `[k v]` pairs sorted ascending by `data/canonical-compare` on `k`; for a set, returns a vector of elements sorted ascending by `data/canonical-compare`. Eliminates guest-UAST $O(n \\log n)$ sorting for `keys`, `vals`, `seq`, `reduce`, and `str`.\n   174\t2. **Boxed IEEE-754 host module `yin.vm.float` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/float.cljc`, module name `'float`):** **Host-boundary conversion rule (r8):** boxed conversion and true-division results are exposed AT the host boundary (`integer/to-float` results and `true-div` quotients enter guest frames only as boxed `data/float64`); the zero-raw-double guarantee is scoped to profiles on the boxed path (the Clojure-family profiles). The frozen native ABI of the legacy preludes is unchanged.\n   175\t   - Operates exclusively on **boxed `data/float64`** inputs and outputs (plus exact integers where specified), returning either a boxed `data/float64`, a boolean/integer/string, or a pure status keyword (`:yin.vm.float/div-zero`, `:yin.vm.float/underflow`, `:yin.vm.float/out-of-range`, `:yin.vm.float/fractional-exp`, `:yin.vm.float/infinite-exp`).\n   176\t   - **Zero raw host doubles in guest UAST:** Because guest code never unwraps a host double across stack frames, `%capture` effects and safepoints can never observe an unwrapped host double — retiring the fragile raw-double leaf-frame rules of r1–r5 completely.\n   177\t   - **Exports (all `:pure`, effects `#{}`):**\n   178\t     - Constants/predicates: `inf`, `neg-inf`, `nan`, `zero`, `neg-zero`, `nan?`, `finite?`, `zero?`, `neg-zero?`, `zero-like`.\n   179\t     - Core IEEE arithmetic: `add`, `sub`, `mul`, `div` (returns boxed IEEE result, or `:yin.vm.float/div-zero` on `div-checked` when `y == 0.0`), `neg` (preserves `-0.0 ↔ +0.0`), `abs`, `compare` (`-1`/`0`/`1` or `:yin.vm.float/nan`).\n   180\t     - Division/floor/power: `floor` (total IEEE double floor), `floor-int` (exact integer for finite `|x| < 2^53`, else `:yin.vm.float/out-of-range`), `fmod-pos` (Sterbenz remainder for finite `x >= 0, y > 0`), `floordiv-mod` (returns `[q r]` boxed pair or `:yin.vm.float/div-zero`, preserving `-0.0` quotient sign and `2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0` rounding correction), `fpow-half` (half-power squaring for `py`/`js`/`clj.py`), `fpow-base` (base squaring for `php`, preserving `1.1 ** 6` bit-exact oracle parity — see D7), `neg-pow` (`[x n pow-order]`, returns boxed `float64` or `:yin.vm.float/underflow`), `parts` (`[mantissa exp2]` exact integer pair).\n   181\t     - Formatting: `format` (deterministic 4-host decimal/scientific formatting over `dao.host.float/float-digits`, rendering `NaN`, `Infinity`, `-Infinity`, `0.0`, `-0.0`, `1.0 -> \"1.0\"` identically on JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt).\n   192\t\n   193\tEvery Layer-2a module follows `yang.core.call`'s single-source dual-emitter pattern: one ordered definition vector emitting both a bundled `uast` (tail-marked) and a linked `module-uast` + `module-spec` (wide-app over stripped definitions, C1-finalized call sites, and `prelude-admission/module-spec`).\n   194\t\n   195\t`yrt.effect` replaces separate `yrt.escape`, `yrt.gen`, and ad-hoc error-callback plumbing with **one composable guest algebraic-effect handler model** over `%capture` and an explicit task-local `ctx-cell`:\n   196\t\n   197\t- **Unified context record:** `{:handlers hs :depth d :base b :frame f}`.\n   198\t  - **4-to-5-slot migration for `js` and `clj`:** In P1, `js/init!`, `clj/init!`, and bundled `yang.clojure` migrate from 4-slot frames to `(yrt.effect/ctx nil 0 0 nil)` and 5-slot frames `[kind payload rest n depth]`:\n   199\t    - `kind`: `:finally` (cleanup frame), `:handler` (abortive exception handler), `:effect` (tagged resumable/abortive effect handler), or any language-installed boundary tag (such as `:generator` during P1→P4 migration).\n   200\t    - `payload`: cleanup closure `fin` (for `:finally`), abortive continuation `r` (for `:handler`), or `[tag handler-fn outer-k]` (for `:effect`).\n   201\t    - `rest`: enclosing frame (or `nil`).\n   202\t    - **`n` (slot 3):** monotonic handler-stack frame count `(+ 1 (frame-depth rest))` for $O(1)$ structural depth comparison (`<= (data/nth hs 3) n`).\n   203\t    - **`depth` (slot 4):** activation-relative call depth restored onto `:depth` by `pop-frame` (`py`/`php` recursion accounting; `0` for `js`/`clj`).\n   204\t- **Capture-safe vector frame reads (`data/nth`):** Every read of the 5-slot frame vector uses **`data/nth`**, reserving `get` strictly for context-map fields (`:handlers`, `:depth`, `:base`). Source-defined `(defn get ...)` can never corrupt frame dispatch.\n   205\t- **Unwind traversal semantics (r8):** `raise` delivers to the first non-`:finally` boundary; on the way down every `:finally` frame runs its cleanup closure **exactly once**, and every `:effect` frame is popped with its context restored (an `:effect` frame carries no cleanup closure — a guest throw crossing an unrelated effect handler is a plain unwind past it, never an error). `perform` walks `ctx-cell` to the nearest matching `:effect` frame **without** running `:finally` frames; only when the handler aborts without resuming does the abort path run the traversed `:finally` cleanups during that unwind. In all cases the context is restored to the surviving frame's state and each cleanup runs at most once per activation.\n   206\t- **`restore!` invariant:** `(fn [ctx-cell saved] (cell/set! ctx-cell (assoc saved :base (get (cell/get ctx-cell) :base))))` — preserves live `:base` across generator/coroutine crossings.\n   207\t\n   208\t**Public exports:**\n   209\t\n   210\t| Category | Export | Signature | Behavior |\n   211\t|---|---|---|---|\n   212\t| **Context & frames** | `ctx`, `handlers`, `set-handlers!`, `restore!`, `frame-depth`, `frame`, `pop-frame` | `[...]` | Stateless context-cell accessors and 5-slot frame constructors (`restore!` preserves live `:base`). |\n   213\t| **Abortive control (exceptions & escapes)** | `raise` | `[ctx-cell e on-empty]` | Unwind `:finally` frames passing `e`; deliver `e` to the first enclosing `:handler` (or non-`:finally` boundary frame); call `(on-empty e)` if empty. |\n   214\t| | `try-value` / `try-orelse` | `[ctx-cell body handler]` / `[ctx-cell body handler orelse]` | Install `:handler`; on normal exit restore and return `(body)` (or tail-call `(orelse)` for `py`/`php`/`clj.py`); on escape restore and call `(handler e)`. |\n   215\t| | `try-finally` | `[ctx-cell body fin normal-arg]` | Install `:finally`; on normal exit restore, run `(fin normal-arg)`, return `v`. |\n   216\t| | `unwind-to` / `call-ec` | `[ctx-cell n normal-arg]` / `[ctx-cell f normal-arg]` | Pop frames down to depth `n` running `:finally` thunks with `normal-arg` (`:py/None`, `:js/undefined`, `:php/null`, `nil`), then restore and jump. |\n   217\t| | `abandon-to` / `call-terminal` | `[ctx-cell n]` / `[ctx-cell f]` | Pop frames down to depth `n` **without** running `:finally` thunks (PHP fatal exit). |\n   218\t| **Resumable & tagged algebraic effects** | `handle` | `[ctx-cell tag handler-fn body]` | Install an `:effect` frame for `tag` around `(body)`. When `(perform ctx-cell tag payload)` fires inside `body`, `yrt.effect` captures the delimited continuation `k`, restores the outer context, and invokes `(handler-fn payload k)` — where `handler-fn` may either abort (returning a value or calling `raise`) or resume `(k v)` one-shot with a computed value. |\n   219\t| | `perform` | `[ctx-cell tag payload on-unhandled]` | Captures the current continuation via `%capture`, walks `ctx-cell` to the nearest matching `:effect` frame for `tag` (without running `:finally` frames unless the handler aborts without resuming), and invokes `(handler-fn payload k)`. If no matching handler exists, calls `(on-unhandled tag payload)`. |\n   220\t\n   249\tTo eliminate ad-hoc `module-spec` and `admit` boilerplate while keeping every runtime dependency completely reproducible and content-pinned, **build-time emission recipes** and **immutable deployment profiles** are separated cleanly.\n   250\t\n   251\t### 5.1 Emission recipe vs. resolved runtime profile\n   252\t\n   253\t1. **`:yang.prelude/recipe` (host-side compiler recipe that *emits* a runtime module):**\n   254\t   ```clojure\n   255\t   {:yang.prelude/schema 1\n   256\t    :yang.prelude/id :yang.python/py-prelude\n   257\t    :yang.prelude/revision \"2026-11-21.1\"\n   258\t    :yang.prelude/module 'py\n   259\t    :yang.prelude/components\n   260\t    [[yang.call \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   261\t     [yrt.effect \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   262\t     [yrt.int \"<blake3-address>\"]]\n   263\t    :yang.prelude/host-modules\n   264\t    {:cell {:required true}\n   265\t     :data {:required true, :min-max-items 1048576}\n   266\t     :integer {:required true, :min-bits 53}\n   267\t     :float {:required true}}\n   268\t    :yang.prelude/emitter\n   269\t    {:mode :linear                 ;; :linear (definitions->uast) | :balanced (balanced-definitions->uast)\n   270\t     :uninit :py/uninit\n   271\t     :rt-namespaces #{\"py.rt\" \"py.b\"}\n   272\t     :unshadow-locals? false\n   273\t     :trailing-requires []         ;; `[]` for base preludes (`py`/`js`/`php`/`clj`/`yang.call`), `['py]`/`['js]` only for safepoint overlays\n   274\t     :finalize-c1? true            ;; annotate `:yang/call-site 1` uniformly across all emitted preludes\n   275\t     :capture-safe-primitives nil} ;; optional for bundled clj mode\n   276\t    :yang.prelude/max-effects nil  ;; optional effect-ceiling set; nil = derive without extra ceiling\n   277\t    :yang.prelude/refusal-ns \"yang.python.antlr\"}\n   278\t   ```\n   279\t2. **`:yang.prelude/profile` (immutable, content-addressed runtime profile after publication):**\n   280\t   Replaces local build knobs with `:yang.prelude/root-address` (the published content address of the owning runtime module) alongside the pinned transitive closure:\n   281\t   ```clojure\n   282\t   {:yang.prelude/schema 1\n   283\t    :yang.prelude/id :yang.python/py-prelude\n   284\t    :yang.prelude/revision \"2026-11-21.1\"\n   285\t    :yang.prelude/module 'py\n   286\t    :yang.prelude/root-address \"<blake3-address-of-published-py-module>\"\n   287\t    :yang.prelude/components\n   288\t    [[yang.call \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   289\t     [yrt.effect \"<blake3-address>\"]\n   290\t     [yrt.int \"<blake3-address>\"]]\n   291\t    :yang.prelude/host-modules\n   292\t    {:cell {:required true}\n   293\t     :data {:required true, :min-max-items 1048576}\n   294\t     :integer {:required true, :min-bits 53}\n   295\t     :float {:required true}}\n   296\t    :yang.prelude/max-effects nil}\n   297\t   ```\n   298\t   A `:yang.prelude/profile` contains zero host functions or closures and passes `yang.frontend/non-portable-path`.\n   299\t\n   300\t### 5.2 Composition rules and verified-closure admission\n   301\t\n   302\t`yang.core.prelude` and `yang.core.prelude-admission` enforce six fail-closed checks. **Home rule (DRY-alignment, r7):** the composition checks (`validate-profile`, `admit-profile`, and their six sub-checks) are implemented in **`yang.core.prelude-admission`** (3 → 5 publics, exactly at the bounded-complexity target), keeping `yang.core.prelude` pure UAST/s-expression emission — the emission/admission boundary is the landed batch-1 seam (`1604aabe`), and the C2 lesson (module duplicating prelude's `host-declaration` was the duplication removed) requires one admission authority, not two namespaces sharing the checks:\n   303\t\n   304\t1. **Verified artifact closure input (`validate-profile`):** Takes `(profile artifact-store registry)`, where `artifact-store` supplies an immutable content-addressed map of published manifests (`manifest-addr -> verified-manifest`) AND their referenced canonical module trees (`tree-addr -> verified-uast`). Verifies that direct root pins match `:yang.prelude/components`, walks the full transitive `:requires` DAG from `:yang.prelude/root-address`, confirms finiteness and acyclicity, and refuses duplicate bindings for the same linker module symbol.\n   305\t2. **Export collision rule (qualified vs. projected):** Distinct Layer-2a/2b/2c modules may share bare local export names across qualified module borders; collisions are refused on duplicate linker module symbols, duplicate stripped local `module-definitions` keys, or duplicate source-facing `:ambient-projections` aliases (`§6.3`).\n   306\t3. **Provenance-door security exclusion (direct declarations, not transitive footprint):** Checks each non-trusted module's (`yrt.*`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core.impl`, `clojure.core`) **direct** `:yin.module/primitives` (refusing `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and `cell/dsg__provenance`) and **direct** `:yin.module/exports` (refusing any `dsg__*` export on **every** module including trusted Layer-2b runtimes), while governing transitive `:yin.module/footprint` through `:yang.prelude/max-effects`.\n   307\t4. **Effect-ceiling verification (`:yang.prelude/max-effects`):** Optional ceiling checked via `(clojure.set/subset? derived-transitive-effects max-effects)` over the verified `:yin.module/footprint :effects` union.\n   308\t5. **Host-module and limit admission (`admit-profile`):** Takes `(profile artifact-store registry host-limits)`, verifies every required host export (`prelude-admission/admit`), and enforces declared numeric floors (`:min-bits`, `:min-digits`, `:min-max-items`) against `host-limits` (failing closed if absent or below floor).\n   309\t6. **Dual-emitter standardization & Parity Law:** Standardized linked emission (`P0`) sets `:trailing-requires []` for base preludes (`['py]`/`['js]` only for safepoint overlays) and `:finalize-c1? true` uniformly. Any program compiled under a composed prelude MUST produce identical outcomes in bundled and linked modes across the semantic, stack, and register VMs (and the AST walker once L-b lands).\n   310\t\n   311\t---\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
