{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '323,343p;371,386p;419,435p;465,489p;510,552p;565,587p;608,628p'\"","aggregated_output":"   323\t\n   324\t### 6.2 Core vs. Frontend ownership boundary\n   325\t\n   326\tTo preserve `yang.antlr.md` §3 (\"Yang core contains no enumeration of supported languages\"):\n   327\t- **`yang.core.semantics` (language-agnostic)** owns ONLY:\n   328\t  1. Generic schema validation for `:yang.semantics/descriptor`.\n   329\t  2. Pure, closed literal-strategy emission (`:raw`, `:float64-raw`, `:tagged-map`, `:raw-or-call`).\n   330\t  3. Generic capability lookup, hook-hygiene validation (every hook must be namespace-qualified), UAST-derived structural export/arity/role verification against the descriptor's **selected, address-verified closure** across **every** executable descriptor field (hooks, executable literal strategies such as `:literals.*.overflow-op`, and ambient projections), and reserved-door projection checks.\n   331\t- **Each parameterized frontend package (e.g. `yang.python.antlr.contract`)** owns:\n   332\t  1. Its **fixed Hook ABI table** (`{hook-key {:arity n :required-by [...]}}`) specifying exact parameter conventions and structural lowering shapes for that frontend's grammar.\n   333\t  2. Structural AST lowering rules marshaling CST operands to those hooks.\n   334\t\n   335\t### 6.3 Portable `:yang.semantics/descriptor` schema\n   336\t\n   337\tA semantics descriptor contains **only portable data** (satisfies `yang.frontend/non-portable-path`):\n   338\t\n   339\t```clojure\n   340\t{:yang.semantics/schema 1\n   341\t :yang.semantics/id :yang.python/clojure-core-v1\n   342\t :yang.semantics/syntax :python\n   343\t :yang.semantics/prelude-module 'clj.py\n   371\t  :control/with         :refused\n   372\t  :oo/classes           :refused\n   373\t  :modules/import       :ambient-only} ;; :supported | :ambient-only | :refused\n   374\t\n   375\t :yang.semantics/literals\n   376\t {:nil     {:kind :raw, :value nil}\n   377\t  :bool    {:kind :raw}\n   378\t  :str     {:kind :raw}\n   379\t  :float   {:kind :float64-raw}      ;; vs {:kind :tagged-map, :tag :py/float}\n   380\t  :int     {:kind :raw-or-call, :safe-max-bits 53, :overflow-op 'clj.py/int-lit}\n   381\t  :unbound {:kind :raw, :value :clj/unbound}}\n   382\t\n   383\t :yang.semantics/hooks\n   384\t {;; Arithmetic & comparisons — ALL namespace-qualified (hygienic, immune to guest shadowing)\n   385\t  :op/add           'clj.py/add\n   386\t  :op/sub           'clj.py/sub\n   419\t  :env/global-set   'clj.py/global-set\n   420\t  ;; Functions & calls\n   421\t  :fn/arg           'clj.py/arg\n   422\t  :fn/make          'clj.py/make-fn\n   423\t  :fn/call          'clj.py/call\n   424\t  ;; Control flow & unit entry (unit/run-main always takes `[body-fn ambient-resolver]`)\n   425\t  :ctrl/for-each    'clj.py/for-each\n   426\t  :ctrl/try         'clj.py/try\n   427\t  :ctrl/try-finally 'clj.py/try-finally\n   428\t  :ctrl/raise       'clj.py/raise\n   429\t  :ctrl/call-ec     'clj.py/call-ec\n   430\t  :unit/run-main    'clj.py/run-main}\n   431\t\n   432\t ;; Each entry defaults to :kind :cell-accessor (emitted per unit into `ambient-resolver` as\n   433\t ;; `(m/e)`, returning the module's stable task-local authenticated callable cell); optional\n   434\t ;; :kind :value references a non-lambda immutable export directly.\n   435\t :yang.semantics/ambient-projections\n   465\t```\n   466\t\n   467\t### 6.4 Validation, lexical hygiene, authority checks, and parameterization\n   468\t\n   469\t1. **Hygienic generated references (no bare hook symbols):** Every non-nil symbol in `:yang.semantics/hooks` and every executable literal-strategy field (such as `:literals.*.overflow-op`) MUST be namespace-qualified (`:yang.semantics/unqualified-hook` otherwise), so user locals named `conj` or `not` can never capture compiler-emitted calls.\n   470\t2. **Scope-aware precedence for `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`:** Free source identifiers resolve in strict order: (1) lexical scope (`:local`, `:cell`, `:nonlocal`), (2) per-module globals (`:vars` in `globals-cell`), (3) unit-bound ambient resolver (`:ambient` in `globals-cell`, passed via `:unit/run-main`), failing with a guest `NameError` on miss.\n   471\t3. **UAST-derived structural export & reserved-door validation (`validate-descriptor`):**\n   472\t   - Takes `(descriptor frontend-contract artifact-store registry)`, computes the descriptor's **selected, address-verified closure**, and inspects every active hook, executable `:literals.*` target, and `:ambient-projections` entry directly against the target manifest's verified `:yin.module/tree` UAST (`wide-app` top-level `(yin/def (quote sym) expr)` definitions):\n   473\t     - **Hooks & executable `:literals.*` targets:** must be namespace-qualified, exported by a module in the selected closure (or required host module checked against `:yin.k/arities`), and defined as a `:lambda` whose parameter count equals `frontend-contract`'s required arity.\n   474\t     - **Ambient projections (`:kind :cell-accessor`):** unique alias names, target `e` is a 0-arg `:lambda` in `m`, and `m` exports 0-arg `init!` and 1-arg `export`.\n   475\t     - **Ambient projections (`:kind :value`):** target `e` is a non-lambda immutable value.\n   476\t     - **Reserved-door ban:** refuses any reference to `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, `yang.safepoint/*`, or `*.impl/*` (`clojure.core.impl/*`).\n   477\t   - Any violation fails closed before reading CST packets with `:yang.semantics/invalid-descriptor`.\n   478\t4. **Address-bound export-role evidence (r8):** qualification, closure membership, and arity alone do not establish a hook's *role* — a binary `clj/prim-get` satisfies an arity check for `:op/add`. The frontend contract or the admitted profile therefore supplies per-hook **role records** (arity + role: `:cell-accessor`, `:value`, operator, projection) resolved by recorded address, and host primitive profiles are resolved by their recorded profile addresses. A same-arity wrong-role target fails closed.\n   479\t5. **Fail-closed capability enforcement during lowering:** Before lowering any guarded CST construct (`classdef`, `yield_expr`, `genexpr`, `with_stmt`, `del_stmt`, typed `except E:`, kwargs, defaults, subscript mutation), lowering checks the descriptor's capability map (with `genexpr` explicitly gated by `:control/generators`) and emits `{:status :refused :reason :yang.semantics/unsupported-capability :capability <cap> :semantics-id <id> :construct <c> :node <id>}` when disabled.\n   480\t6. **Frontend parameterization:** `yang.python.antlr.lower`, `yang.typescript.antlr.lower`, and `yang.php.antlr.lower` read literals, hooks (including 2-arg `:unit/run-main [body-fn ambient-resolver]` and optional `:comp/finish`), capabilities, and projections from `:yang.semantics/descriptor`, preserving full CPython/Node/PHP oracle and 4-host parity under the legacy pins. **Entry-lowering contracts (r8):** each frontend's contract specifies BOTH entry shapes — the landed native entry shape (`py/run-main` 1-arg, `js` single-operand, `php` 2-or-4 with the request stream in slot two) for the legacy track, and the Clojure profile's resolver-bearing 2-arg `[body-fn ambient-resolver]` shape — so the native mapping is 1:1 against the FROZEN exports and never re-arches them to satisfy the Clojure profile. **Oracle assignment (r8):** native-oracle parity suites gate the LEGACY pins; capability-refusal suites gate the default profile.\n   481\t\n   482\t### 6.5 Frontend SPI and provenance integration (`yang.frontend`)\n   483\t\n   484\tNo `yang.frontend` schema change is required (`src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc`):\n   485\t- `:yang.frontend/id` names the frontend syntax + lowering implementation (e.g., `:yang.python/antlr`), and each profile gets an immutable `:yang.frontend/revision` (`\"py-v1\"` vs. `\"clojure-core-v1\"`).\n   486\t- `:yang.frontend/lowering-profile` pins the content address of the `:yang.semantics/descriptor` EDN artifact; `:yang.frontend/runtime-profile` pins the resolved `:yang.prelude/profile` manifest. **Descriptor/runtime reconciliation (r8):** where two lowerer revisions consume one descriptor, the pins are reconciled **by module symbol before lowering** — a conflicting pin fails closed. Dependency-first module installation belongs to linked composition (a verified dependency pin does not install its module in a cold task; first execution on a cold task is gated). The resolver's derivation is recorded in provenance; its live cell is task-owned.\n   487\t- Compilation provenance retains the exact derivation record (r8: frontend/lowerer revision, descriptor, resolved runtime closure, input, output).\n   488\t- **Default selector (r8):** the composition's immutable configuration carries the preferred `[frontend-id revision]` pair, applied at the normal request entry; `yang.frontend/select`'s ID-only ambiguity resolves through that configuration. Gates: both revisions installed → ordinary request selects Clojure semantics; explicit legacy pin → native behavior preserved; in-flight request → original snapshot retained.\n   489\t\n   510\t\n   511\t*Truth-in-advertising invariant:* `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` explicitly declares Clojure truthiness, persistent immutable collections, non-numeric booleans, and kind-strict equality as its support profile — never CPython parity.\n   512\t\n   513\t### 7.2 Portable numeric & collection contract (`clj.py` over `:pure` host core + `yrt.effect`)\n   514\t\n   515\tBecause the Tier-1 `:pure` host core (`yin.vm.data`, `yin.vm.integer`, `yin.vm.float`) handles all host-representation details natively, `clj.py` becomes a thin, readable adapter:\n   516\t\n   517\t1. **Portable kind classification (`clj.py/num-kind`):**\n   518\t   ```clojure\n   519\t   (if (integer/integer? x)\n   520\t     :int\n   521\t     (if (data/float64? x) :float :other))\n   522\t   ```\n   523\t   Non-numeric operands raise `{:clj.py/error :type-error ...}` via `clj/raise` (in `v1`, string `+` concatenates via `data/str-concat`; `*` is strictly numeric).\n   524\t2. **Int × Int:** Delegates directly to `yin.vm.integer` (`add`, `sub`, `neg`, `mul`, `floor-div-mod`, `pow`, `true-div`, `compare`), checking `b == 0` beforehand (performing `:math/div-zero`) and passing every result through `yrt.int/check-limit` before indexing `[q r]` pairs or chaining into further ops. Negative integer exponents promote `a` via `integer/to-float` + `data/float64` and delegate to `float/neg-pow` (`:half`), performing `:math/overflow` if `:yin.vm.float/underflow` is returned.\n   525\t3. **Float × Float and Mixed Int × Float:**\n   526\t   - Exact ints promote via `(data/float64 (yrt.int/check-limit (clj/rt-ctx) (integer/to-float-boxed i)))` — `integer/to-float-boxed` (r8) returns the boxed carrier at the host boundary so no raw host double crosses a guest frame.\n   527\t   - `+`, `-`, `*`, unary `-`, unary `+`, `/`, `//`, `%`, `**`, and `<`/`<=`/`>`/`>=` delegate directly to boxed `yin.vm.float` exports (`float/add`, `float/sub`, `float/mul`, `float/neg`, `float/div-checked`, `float/floordiv-mod`, `float/fpow-half`, `float/neg-pow`, `float/compare`) and `integer/compare-float` (via boxed float helper).\n   528\t   - Cold status keywords (`:yin.vm.float/div-zero`, `:yin.vm.float/underflow`, `:yin.vm.float/fractional-exp`, `:yin.vm.float/infinite-exp`) are translated by `clj.py`'s effect handler into guest error maps (`{:clj.py/error :zero-division ...}`, `:overflow`, `:pow-fractional`, `:pow-infinite`) via `yrt.effect/perform` → `clj/raise`.\n   529\t4. **Uniform key admission & equality:**\n   530\t   - **Key/element admission:** Map/set construction and lookup in both `clj.py` and `clojure.core.impl` call `(data/admit-key? k)` once; on `false`, perform `:coll/unsupported-key` (raising `{:clj.py/error :unsupported-key :key k}` or `ex-info`).\n   531\t   - **Equality:** `clj.py/eq` delegates directly to **`data/equiv`**; `clj.py/ne` delegates to `(not (data/equiv a b))`.\n   532\t   - **Deterministic traversal:** Map/set iteration delegates directly to **`data/canonical-entries`**.\n   533\t\n   534\t### 7.3 Python lowering Hook ABI & `clj.py` adapters\n   535\t\n   536\t| Hook key | Frontend ABI signature | `clj.py` implementation |\n   537\t|---|---|---|\n   538\t| `:env/local-get` | `[cell name]` | Reads `(cell/get cell)`; raises guest unbound error if `:clj/unbound`. |\n   539\t| `:env/global-get` | `[globals-cell name]` | Checks `(data/contains? (get g :vars) name)` first; on miss invokes unit-owned `((get g :ambient) name)`; if `:clj/unbound`, raises guest `NameError` map built via evaluated `assoc`. |\n   540\t| `:env/global-set` | `[globals-cell name value]` | Updates `:vars` in `globals-cell` (preserving `:ambient`) and returns `value`. |\n   541\t| `:fn/make` | `[fname spec defaults kwdefaults code]` | Accepts the 5 arguments from `yang.python.antlr.lower/function-value:1870`; delegates to trusted Layer-2b **`clj/make-callable`** (`§7.4`). |\n   542\t| `:fn/call` | `[callee args]` | Delegates to trusted Layer-2b **`clj/invoke-callable`** (`§7.4`). Zero provenance doors inside `clj.py`. |\n   543\t| `:ctrl/try` | `[body handler orelse]` | Calls `yrt.effect/try-orelse` on `(clj/rt-ctx)`. |\n   544\t| `:ctrl/try-finally` | `[body fin]` | Calls `yrt.effect/try-finally` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` with `normal-arg = nil`. |\n   545\t| `:ctrl/raise` | `[e]` | Calls `clj/raise` (delegating to `yrt.effect/raise` on `(clj/rt-ctx)`). |\n   546\t| `:ctrl/call-ec` | `[f]` | Calls `yrt.effect/call-ec` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` with `normal-arg = nil`. |\n   547\t| `:ctrl/for-each` | `[iterable step-fn]` | Invokes `clojure.core.impl/impl-seq`, `impl-first`, `impl-rest` (backed by `data/canonical-entries` for maps/sets), raises guest error on non-collection iterables, and invokes `step-fn` per element. |\n   548\t| `:comp/list-new`, `:comp/set-new`, `:comp/dict-new` | `[init-vec]`, `[]`, `[]` | Allocates temporary local accumulator cell holding persistent `[]`, `#{}`, or `{}`. |\n   549\t| `:comp/list-append`, `:comp/set-add`, `:comp/dict-set` | `[acc val]`, `[acc val]`, `[acc k v]` | Validates set elements / dict keys via `data/admit-key?`, updates persistent value inside `acc`, returns `nil`. |\n   550\t| `:comp/finish` | `[acc]` *(optional)* | Returns `(cell/get acc)` (omitted/`nil` in `:yang.python/py-v1`). |\n   551\t| `:unit/run-main` | `[body-fn ambient-resolver]` | Calls idempotent `(clj/init!)`, `(clojure.core/init!)`, `(clj.py/init!)`; installs `clj.py`'s cold-effect policy handlers (`:math/*`, `:int/*`, `:coll/unsupported-key`) on `(clj/rt-ctx)`; allocates a fresh per-unit `globals` cell; invokes `(body-fn globals globals-fn)` and returns the value verbatim without stripping `[:yin.k/ok ...]`. |\n   552\t\n   565\t  - *Step D:* Run argument binding + body inside **`yrt.effect/try-value`** on `(clj/rt-ctx)`. Normal exit restores `(clj/rt-ctx)` and returns the value verbatim; escape inspects private `(cell/dsg__provenance e)` to forward retained protocol conditions without double-wrapping or wrap user escapes via `(yang.call/thrown e)`.\n   566\t- **Call-site boundary (`clj/invoke-callable`):** Checks `clj/admitted-callable?` (minting retained `:yang.call/not-callable` on failure), else calls `yang.call/invoke` with a `raise-exit` that unwraps `:yang.call/thrown` and retains all other protocol conditions via private `cell/dsg__new-provenance`.\n   567\t\n   568\t### 7.5 Two-module portable `clojure.core` contract (`clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core`)\n   569\t\n   570\tIn Slice P3, the portable Clojure standard library splits into two Layer-2c linker modules — eliminating store-key collisions against VM primitives while publishing cell-free 0-arg export accessors:\n   571\t\n   572\t1. **`clojure.core.impl` (pure, stateless implementation module — banned from `:ambient-projections`):**\n   573\t   - Requires `yang.call`, `clj`, `yrt.int` (zero direct provenance doors; **zero state cells — but it DECLARES its runtime effects**: the `:coll/unsupported-key` and `:int/*` effects its definitions perform are part of its declared footprint, installed by the owning entry's policy handlers — `clj.py/run-main` at P3′, plain `yang.clojure`'s own cold-error policy at P2′). Host dependencies: `kind` (with `kind/namespace`), `data` (with `float64?`, `equiv`, `admit-key?`, `canonical-compare`, `canonical-entries`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), `float`, and `cell` (for cell checks/updates only).\n   574\t   - **Zero bare primitive store collisions:** Every definition is prefixed `impl-*` (`impl-identity`, `impl-get`, `impl-assoc`, `impl-conj`, etc.), so internal calls to `(get m k)`, `(assoc m k v)`, `(conj xs x)`, `(first xs)`, `(rest xs)`, `(vec xs)`, `(nil? x)`, `(empty? xs)`, `(not b)` resolve directly to VM primitives.\n   575\t   - **Cell-safe collection predicates:** `impl-cell-ref?` ensures authenticated callable cells answer **`false`** to all of `coll?`, `map?`, `set?`, `vector?`, `sequential?`, `seq?`, `list?`, and `reduced?`; `impl-fn?` matches `clj/admitted-callable?` 1-to-1.\n   576\t   - **Host-backed portable operations (zero guest-UAST leak workarounds):**\n   577\t     - `impl-inc`, `impl-dec`, `impl-rem`, `impl-int?`: delegate to `integer/*` + `yrt.int/check-limit` and `float/add`/`float/sub`.\n   578\t     - `impl-not=`: delegates to `(not (data/equiv a b))`.\n   579\t     - `impl-str`: deterministic renderer delegating ints to `integer/format`, floats to `float/format`, keywords/symbols to `kind/namespace` + `kind/name`, maps/sets to `data/canonical-entries`, and authenticated cells to `\"#<fn>\"`.\n   580\t     - `impl-seq`, `impl-first`, `impl-rest`, `impl-vec`, `impl-keys`, `impl-vals`, `impl-reduce`, `impl-map`, `impl-filter`, `impl-remove`, `impl-into`, `impl-merge`, `impl-union`, `impl-difference`: normalize maps/sets via `data/canonical-entries`.\n   581\t     - Map/set mutators and lookups (`impl-assoc`, `impl-get`, `impl-contains?`, `impl-conj`, `impl-disj`, `impl-merge`, `impl-into`, etc.): enforce `data/admit-key?`.\n   582\t     - Explicitly excluded: `var?`, `resolve`, `invoke-value`.\n   583\t2. **Public cell-free facade `clojure.core` (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/core_module.cljc`):**\n   584\t   - Requires `clj` and `clojure.core.impl`. Exports only cell-free pure functions at install time: idempotent 0-arg `init!` (building `{sym cell}` with `clj/prim-assoc` and `clj/make-callable`), 1-arg `export` (using `clj/prim-get`), and 0-arg cell-accessor exports `(fn [] (clojure.core/export (quote <name>)))`.\n   585\t   - Dynamic closures (`impl-comp`, `impl-partial`) construct cells via `clj/make-callable`; all dynamic callbacks (`map`, `filter`, `reduce`, `update`, etc.) invoke via `clj/invoke-callable`.\n   586\t   - **Direct `yang.clojure` migration in P3:** Retires `yang.clojure`'s inline `library-for` duplication and unit-local `dsg__call_token` path so there is one unified Clojure runtime.\n   587\t\n   608\t### 8.1 Multi-host portability (JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, Jolt/Scheme)\n   609\t\n   610\t- **ClojureDart AOT literal limits:** Consolidate `defquoted` into **`yang.core.defquoted`** (r8 M9 — the dedicated host macro namespace; NOT `yang.core.prelude`, keeping the emission namespace free of macro definitions).\n   611\t- **Zero bare integral float literals & zero raw host doubles in guest UAST:** All float operations pass boxed `data/float64` through `yin.vm.float`, avoiding raw host doubles across JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt.\n   612\t- **Canonical ordering (`b86bc0e8` invariant):** Recipes, profiles, descriptor maps, and emitted UAST operand sequences sort keys deterministically, guaranteeing byte-identical `dao.jing.cbor` hashes across all 4 hosts.\n   613\t- **No JVM-only reflection:** `yang.core.semantics` and `yang.core.prelude` use pure portable Clojure data transforms.\n   614\t\n   615\t### 8.2 Dependency graph and malleability (`docs/agents/malleability.md`)\n   616\t\n   617\tVerified with `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` (r7: the analyzer's high-degree predicate now counts combined in+out degree ≥ 6, matching this document's rule; `56d17563`). No multi-node cycles and no multi-node SCCs exist. The analyzer prints three SELF-loop warnings (`yang.php.antlr.quoted`, `yang.python.antlr.prelude`, `yang.typescript.antlr.prelude` — macro self-reference in defquoted-family namespaces); these are analyzer-reporting artifacts, not runtime dependency cycles, and are expected to disappear once the defquoted consolidation (P0) lands:\n   618\t\n   619\t```text\n   620\tLayer A (AST & Data Schemas):    yang.core.uast\n   621\tLayer B (Pure Composition):      yang.core.prelude, yang.core.semantics, yang.core.defquoted (P0 host macro ns)\n   622\tLayer C (Registry Admission):    yang.core.prelude-admission, yang.core.module, yang.core.publication\n   623\tLayer D (Guest linker modules,  yrt.effect, yrt.int, yrt.safepoint, yang.call — emitted UAST\n   624\t  emitted from host code):        artifacts consumed at runtime on every backend\n   625\tLayer D' (Host emitter ns for   src/cljc/yang/rt/{effect,int,safepoint}.cljc — clojure namespaces\n   626\t  the D-layer modules):           requiring yang.core.prelude/prelude-admission/core.call\n   627\tLayer E (Language Frontends):    yang.python.antlr.*, yang.typescript.antlr.*, yang.php.antlr.*,\n   628\t                                 yang.clojure.{prelude, core-impl, core-module}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
