{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '14,18p' docs/design/yang.preludes.md | fold -sw 165 && rg -n 'sort map keys|Sort map keys' docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md\"","aggregated_output":"- **2026-11-21 (r5 → r6 hybrid architecture & focused profile scope):** Eliminated guest-UAST host-leak workarounds and collapsed fragmented control subsystems \ninto a **three-tier hybrid model** (aligned with Unison, Koka, and OCaml 5): (1) promoted representation-sensitive pure ops (`data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, \n`data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `data/admit-key?`, `kind/namespace`, and boxed IEEE-754 `yin.vm.float`) into `:pure` host primitives backed by \n`dao.jing.cbor` / `dao.host.*`, eliminating raw-double stack-frame hazards and guest-side $O(n \\log n)$ sorting; (2) unified `yrt.escape`, `yrt.gen`, safepoint \ninterrupt dispatch, and cold error/limit policy traps into one composable guest algebraic-effect layer (`yrt.effect`) over `%capture` with zero Jolt kernel \nexpansion; (3) focused swappable preludes on **Native profiles** (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj` for existing code in those languages) plus **N → 1 Yin/Clojure \nprofiles** (`yang.python/clojure-core-v1`, future `yang.typescript/clojure-core-v1`), dropping unnecessary off-diagonal N×M symmetry (such as \n`:yang.clojure/py-v1`).\n- **2026-11-21 (r7 → r8 reconciliation):** Addressed all findings from the r7 architect review (thread `01a1faa3-bb7e-7c30-b3bf-cedbad008bfc`; 8 HIGH, 1 MEDIUM, \nplus default-profile regressions): (H1) explicit default-selector mechanism — the composition's immutable configuration carries the preferred `[id revision]`, \napplied at the normal request entry, with two-revision / legacy-pin / in-flight-snapshot gates; (H2) per-frontend **entry-lowering contracts** emitting the landed \nnative entry shapes (`py` 1-arg `run-main`, `js` 1-operand, `php` 2-or-4 with request stream) alongside the Clojure resolver-bearing 2-arg shape; (H3) ONE \nderivation record (frontend/lowerer revision, descriptor, resolved runtime closure, input, output), pins reconciled by module symbol before lowering, \ndependency-first installation in linked composition, resolver derivation in provenance / live cell in the task; (H4) complete effect-unwind traversal per frame kind \nwith exactly-once cleanup, a P2′ cold-error policy for plain `yang.clojure`, `clojure.core.impl` owning zero cells while declaring its runtime effects; (H5) \naddress-bound export-**role** evidence (same-arity wrong-role fails closed); (H6) the §5.1 example labeled a Track B recipe recording bundled shape, linked \ntrailing forms, pins, and C1 behavior independently; (H7) slice repair — P1′ clj-only synthetic fixtures, P2′ native collection invocation + bundled \nshadowing, P3′ the real cross-syntax unwind; (H8) boxed conversion/true-division at the host boundary, zero-raw-double scoped to boxed-path profiles; (M9) \n`yang.core.defquoted` naming consistency, r6 gates attached verbatim to Track B, oracle assignment (legacy pins ← native oracles, default ← capability \nrefusals); (R) default-profile regressions — unqualified `:k` admission, cross-carrier integer identity, `:clj/unbound` distinguishability, canonical order \nsettled to Jing encoded-byte order.\n- **2026-11-21 (r6 → r7 Clojure-First Default & Legacy Track, plus landed-DRY reconciliation):** Three owner directives. **(D10) Default-profile inversion:** for \n`yang.python` (and later `yang.typescript`/`yang.php`), the **N → 1 Yin/Clojure profile is the DEFAULT** runtime profile; the native preludes (`py`/`js`/`php` \nsemantics) become the **Legacy compatibility track** — kept frozen as landed (they already exist, oracle-parity-proven, at their current content addresses), with \ntheir *re-architecture* onto `yrt.*`/boxed float deferred until legacy demand justifies it. **(Clojure-first roadmap):** the implementation order re-sequenced so \nthe Clojure prelude family (`yrt.effect`/`yrt.int` with Clojure-only consumers, unified trusted `clj`, `clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core` facade, `clj.py`, the \npython lowerer's descriptor parameterization) is built FIRST — the other-language native preludes are untouched by those slices (zero golden churn; defquoted \nconsolidation and emitter standardization for py/ts/php defer to the legacy track). **(DRY-alignment reconciliation):** §5.2 admission checks home in \n`yang.core.prelude-admission` (3→5 publics, at bound) keeping `yang.core.prelude` pure emission; §8.2 names both the guest linker modules (`yrt.*`) and their \nhost emitter namespaces (`src/cljc/yang/rt/*.cljc`) and acknowledges the analyzer's 3 self-loop warnings (macro self-reference, no multi-node cycles); defquoted \nconsolidation accounted against the public-surface ledger; §2 gains the tao-architecture second-axiom alignment (the semantics descriptor is stream-resident \ninterpreter configuration; the provenance tuple names the interpreter).\n\n**Authority:** Subordinate to [`datom.world.md`](./datom.world.md) (axioms, invariants, streams, host boundaries), \n[`adr/0004-external-effects-are-interpreted-stream-deposits.md`](./adr/0004-external-effects-are-interpreted-stream-deposits.md) (external effects as stream \ndeposits), [`yang.antlr.md`](./yang.antlr.md) (§3 frontend SPI, §8.1–§8.2 semantic placement, §8.5.5 float addresses, §8.5.6 linked modules, §8.10 shared \ncalling convention, §8.11 cells, §9 four-layer stdlib model), [`yang.typescript.md`](./yang.typescript.md) (§2.2 shared rulings, §17 lift enumeration, §19 \nowner decision A12.5), [`yang.php.md`](./yang.php.md) (§9 prelude inventory), [`yin.vm.linker.md`](./yin.vm.linker.md), \n[`yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`](./yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md), [`dao.jing.cbor.md`](./dao.jing.cbor.md), and \n[`src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md`](../../src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md).\n173:- Normalize sorted collections to ordinary maps and sets. Sort map keys\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
