rn), with their `yrt.*`/boxed-float re-architecture deferred to the legacy track (Track B). The orig\n643:| Slice | Scope & deliverables | Golden impact | Concrete acceptance gate |\n645:| **P0′ — Composition plumbing & `:pure` host core extensions** | Implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` / `:yang.prelude/profile`, `validate-profile` + `admit-profile` **in `yang.core.prelude-admission`** (3→5 publics, per the §5.2 home rule); add `:pure` host exports (`data/float64?`, `data/e\n646:| **P1′ — `yrt.effect` + `yrt.int` with Clojure-only consumers; unified trusted `clj`** | Implement stateless `yrt.effect` (5-slot `data/nth` frames, abortive `raise`/`try-value`/`try-orelse`/`try-finally`/`call-ec`, plus resumable `handle`/`perform` — the frame design anticipates py/php `\n647:| **P2′ — Unified `clojure.core` + `yang.clojure` migration** | Publish collision-free `clojure.core.impl` (pure, `impl-*` prefix, `admit-key?`-guarded) + cell-free `clojure.core` facade; migrate `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core`. | Refresh `yang.clojure` goldens cl\n648:| **P3′ — Descriptor parameterization + `clj.py` + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (the DEFAULT flip)** | Implement generic `yang.core.semantics` with UAST-derived arity & role validation; define the python frontend contract; refactor `yang.python.antlr.lower` to read literals/hooks/capabilit\n649:| **P4′ — Additional N → 1 profiles** | `:yang.typescript/clojure-core-v1` next (descriptor + ts frontend contract); `:yang.php/clojure-core-v1` after. | Fresh goldens per profile | End-to-end parity suites per profile. |\n650:| **Track B — Legacy prelude re-architecture (deferred, on demand)** | Migrate the native `py`/`js`/`php` preludes onto `yrt.effect`/`yrt.int`/boxed float (the r6 P1/P4 legs: 4→5-slot contexts, generators via `:gen/yield`, `yrt.safepoint`, `php.sp` integration per its own hooks); undertaken \n658:   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* `:mutation/locals :cell` (task-heap cells holding pure persistent Clojure values, matching Python parameter binding, unbound reads, reassignment, loops, and `nonlocal` with per-module `globals` cells). Keep `:single-assignment` as a separate\n666:4. **D4 — Golden migration policy (`Settled — Owner Clean-Slate Directive`):**\n667:   - Settled in favor of clean golden regeneration per slice (`P0`–`P4`), preserving correctness via behavioral, 4-host, and language-oracle suites rather than frozen-quirk backwards compatibility.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
