{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-20 20:35:43 GMT  \nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-21 03:35:43 +07\n\n**H1 is resolved.** The composition owns the preferred `[frontend-id revision]` and applies it at normal request entry. The three gates cover both revisions installed, an explicit legacy override, and an in-flight request retaining its snapshot. This preserves the catalog’s existing ambiguity rule and requires no closed language registry. [§6.5](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:488)\n\nI reread r8 from disk. Several corrections appear in the revision history and in new paragraphs while the corresponding ABI, emitter rule, or acceptance table still requires the old behavior.\n\n| Severity | Section | Evidence | Correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **High** | H2 · §§6.2–6.4 | The entry-lowering paragraph correctly distinguishes native and Clojure call shapes and assigns native oracles to legacy pins. Admission still compares the export’s lambda parameter count to one required arity. Frozen PHP exposes a four-parameter lambda that lowering legitimately calls with two **or** four operands. [Admission rule](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:473) · [PHP export](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:5866) · [PHP calls](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3938) | Record the verified export signature and the permitted emitted call shapes separately for each entry contract. Qualify the “always takes” two-argument comment to `clj.py`. Gate both PHP modes, including observable stream output. |\n| **Medium** | H3 · §§2.1–2.1a, 6.5 | The new derivation record includes the lowerer revision. Linked composition owns dependency-first installation, and the live resolver is task-owned. The earlier normative tuple still lists both `lowering-profile` and `semantics-descriptor`, even though §6.5 assigns them the same address. That tuple omits the lowerer revision. [Earlier tuple](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:65) · [New record](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:78) | Reference the §6.5 record throughout. Require descriptor/runtime pin reconciliation on every compilation, including a single lowerer revision paired with a conflicting runtime pin. |\n| **High** | H4 · §§4.3, 7.5 | The new prose says `raise` pops an `:effect` frame. The public ABI still permits delivery to any non-`:finally` boundary, which includes that same frame. Plain Clojure now owns a P2′ cold-error policy. However, §7.5 puts guest policy tags such as `:coll/unsupported-key` into the declared footprint. The linker derives that footprint from VM operations, primitive profiles, and dependencies. [Unwind rule](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:205) · [Public ABI](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:213) · [Footprint derivation](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:81) | Give `raise` one rule per frame kind. Gate a throw past an unrelated effect frame with exactly-once cleanup. Keep guest policy tags in the handler contract and declare the underlying VM effects through the existing linker mechanism. |\n| **Medium** | H5 · §6.4 | R8 requires address-resolved role evidence, host profile resolution, and same-arity wrong-role refusal. The record description still allows the broad role `operator`. Two binary operators in the same published module can share the module address, arity, and that role. [Role evidence](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:478) | Make the authorization key explicit as `(module address, export symbol, exact hook or projection role)`. Apply it to executable literal targets too. Gate substitution of subtraction for addition within the same module. |\n| **High** | H6 · §§5.1–5.2, P0′ | Only the revision history labels the Python example Track B. The recipe itself has `:trailing-requires []`, `:finalize-c1? true`, and `yrt.*` pins. §5.2 still mandates uniform emission in P0. Landed Python ends its module tree with `require yang.call`. P0′ also still calls the Clojure-family bundle balanced, although its continuation emitter uses a left fold. [Recipe](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:253) · [P0 rule](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:309) · [Python tree](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc:4111) · [Clojure emitter](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:994) | Label the example at its definition and scope standardization to Track B. Gate each frozen runtime’s bundled shape, linked tree and manifest addresses, dependency pins, and C1 side-table identity or absence. |\n| **High** | H7 · §9 | P1′ now has the synthetic depth/base fixture and correctly says the real cross-syntax unwind belongs in P3′. The **P2′ acceptance row still requires that unwind**, one slice before `clj.py` exists. The native migration also still excludes `invoke-value`, while an existing fixture calls a locally bound map. [Slice table](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:646) · [Excluded operation](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:582) · [Native fixture](/tmp/preludes-r7/test/yang/clojure_test.clj:3197) | Put native collection invocation and bundled primitive shadowing in the P2′ row, and specify how native data calls dispatch. Put the real `clj → clj.py → clj` unwind and context-restoration gate solely in P3′. |\n| **High** | H8 · §§2.2, 4.1, 7.2 | Mixed promotion now uses `integer/to-float-boxed`. The adjacent negative-exponent path still calls raw `integer/to-float`, and integer division still passes the landed `true-div` result through guest `check-limit`. Both paths can expose a raw result before boxing. The global invariant also still promises safety “everywhere.” [Numeric paths](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:524) · [Landed exports](/tmp/preludes-r7/src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc:414) · [Invariant](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:91) | Use boxed host exports on all three Clojure-family paths. Scope the invariant to those profiles and gate integral float and negative-zero results across capture and restore. |\n| **High** | Default-profile regressions · §§4.1, 6.3, 7.2–7.3 | P3′ lists all four requested fixtures. Yet `local-get` and the ambient resolver still interpret a returned `:clj/unbound` as absence. That directly fails the new fixture. `admit-key?` still requires a nonempty namespace, and its boolean result cannot normalize distinct integer carriers before a host map operation. Jing encoded-byte order is now explicit, although the added recursive element-order clause can disagree with it for different-length vectors. [Key rules](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:171) · [Lookup](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:530) · [Binding reads](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:538) · [Fixtures](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:648) | Carry presence independently of the payload for locals and projections. Allow an absent namespace, normalize integer keys recursively on insertion and lookup, and use encoded bytes as the single ordering rule for compound keys. |\n\n**M9 is substantially reconciled.** `yang.core.defquoted` is consistent across §8 and P0′. Track B now lists its generator, safepoint, cleanup, concurrency, bundled/linked, four-host, and native-oracle gates directly. I could verify their presence in r8. The worktree contains no separate r6 gate table for a verbatim comparison. [Macro home](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:610) · [Track B gates](/tmp/preludes-r7/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:650)\n\nThis was a read-only design review. No implementation or acceptance suites were run for r8.\n\nARCHITECT VERDICT: CHANGES REQUIRED - the frozen-emitter rule, P2′ gate, unwind ABI, boxed numeric paths, and binding semantics still contradict their stated corrections."}}
